55,"C_source":"Mean difference between the Santander tide gauge (IOC san2), tied to NMMA, and the tide level of this map, at 51 of its 117 images","attribution":"MAREA products by the authors of the MAREA project (see CITATION.cff in the repository), CC BY 4.0. Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel-2 data processed in the Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem. Tide: EOT20 (Hart-Davis et al., 2021, Earth System Science Data 13, 3869-3884; CC BY 4.0) and, where stated, sea-level records of the IOC Sea Level Station Monitoring Facility (VLIZ/IOC-UNESCO).","crs":"EPSG:4326","datums":"EOT20 tide model at the site, 19 years (2007-2025) every 10 min. LAT and HAT: its lowest and highest levels. MSL: its mean. MLWS, MLWN, MHWN and MHWS: the means of its tidal-day low and high waters on spring and on neap days.","description":"Contours of the MAREA elevation map at the tidal datums of the site.","drawn":"A datum is drawn only between the 1st and 99th percentiles of the mapped heights, inside the automatic intertidal mask.","level_m":"m above the mean sea level of the tide model at the site (the zero of the map heights)","level_nmma_m":"m above NMMA (mean sea level at Alicante): level_m + C","licence":"CC BY 4.0","map":"MAREA elevation from 117 Sentinel-2 images (2021-2026), inside the automatic intertidal mask, smoothed with a 10 m Gaussian; lines of 100 m or more, simplified to 2.5 m.","preliminary":"Preliminary: the mask was made by a rule and not checked by hand, and these elevations have no accuracy assessment (no survey of the ground at this site).","site":"san_vicente","title":"Tide lines","units":"m"},"name":"tide_lines","type":"FeatureCollection"}
